description:
I'm mirroring this folder to another device one way. I've modified a file on the other device so syncing stops and I see:

![image](/uploads/a344c09d2c49044d5db87175b69c05ea/image.png){width=900 height=416}


But the qs shows syncing is at 100%. Would be nice if the QS would indicate the out-of-sync state.

With a device where the cutouts are lower than the top bar (PHOSH_TOP_BAR_HEIGHT = 32px), the cutout eats into the application and doesn't fit fully in the top bar.

Ideally if the cutout get's lower than the top bar height, the top bar height is adjusted to fit again.

E.g. nothing,spacewar:

![image](/uploads/51d33a853857458779bfce78cbe14828/image.png){width=835 height=268}

Or fairphone,fp5:

![image](/uploads/522b2440af66b859969a5beb8dea640f/image.png){width=900 height=248}
